<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market intervention.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market intervention.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from intervening in the open market on Monday, the New York Fed confirmed.</p>
<p>The no-action was a mild surprise.  While some analysts predicted seven-day system repurchase agreements to meet a $5.0 billion to $6.0 billion add need this period, others said the Fed's aggressiveness in the open market last week took care of this session's add need.</p>
<p>Federal funds were somewhat tight, trading at 5-9/16 percent, above the 5-1/2 percent target rate.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
